From: Nicolas Villar <15879262+nvillar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 11:44:03 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Duo: the first tap on an editor in the other panel shows the
 keyboard

A tap on an editor in a window that does not have window focus, the app on the other panel, is delivered (down and up)
before the focus change it causes reaches the app. The window manager moves focus on the down
(handlePointerDownOutsideFocus -> setFocusedTask), but the focus event arrives about 90 ms later (gate G5: up at
+10 ms, onWindowFocusChanged at +92 ms). On the up the editor takes view focus and calls showSoftInput while its window
is not the input method manager's current root: the view is not served and the request is dropped
(InputMethodManager.showSoftInput, "Ignoring showSoftInput() as view=... is not served"). The window then gains focus
with a focused editor, which shows nothing by itself (SOFT_INPUT_STATE_UNSPECIFIED without forward navigation;
ImeVisibilityStateComputer only restores the keyboard for a window that had it before). With refactor_insets_controller
the keyboard follows the requested visibility of its control target, so a keyboard up for the other panel went away
with its control (gate G5.ime.B.fromA: shown on the new panel, then hidden within 70 ms) and a hidden one stayed hidden
(G5.ime.A.editor1 rep 1). The user had to tap a second time (ledger F10). The reverse direction passed only because the
target window had shown the keyboard before (restore).

While the two panel policy is active (sys.duode.panels.active=1), a show request that is not served because the
requesting view is the focused view of a window without window focus, on the default display, is remembered (weakly,
with its flags and time); a later hide request from the process drops it.
When the next window of this process gains focus and has started input, the request is replayed if that window's
focused view is the requesting view, it still has focus, and the request is at most 1 s old; it is dropped otherwise.
The replay is an ordinary showSoftInput from the now served view. Nothing changes with the policy off, or for a
request from a focused window.

Not built or run on a device yet. Verified by git am -3 after the series and a javac type check against the gate
build's framework jar.

Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
